    {
      "title": "Primitives vs Reference Types",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Primitives vs Reference Types",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. The Two Families",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**7 primitives**: ==string, number, bigint, boolean, undefined, null, symbol==",
                "Everything else is an ==object==: arrays, functions, dates, maps"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Copy vs Share",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Primitives are ==immutable==; `let b = a` is an independent copy",
                "Objects are stored ==by reference==: `b.x = 1` changes `a.x` too",
                "`s[0]='X'` is ignored in sloppy mode, {red:TypeError} in strict (modules, classes)"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "let a = 1, b = a; b = 2;",
                "const o = {x: 0}, p = o; p.x = 1;",
                "console.log(a, o.x, [1] === [1]);"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "output",
              "lines": [
                "1 1 false"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Compare and Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Primitives",
                "Objects"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`let b = a`",
                  "independent copy",
                  "one shared object"
                ],
                [
                  "`===`",
                  "by value: `'a'==='a'` true",
                  "by identity: `{}==={}` false"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`const o = {}; o.x = 1` works: `const` freezes the binding only",
                "`{...o}` is shallow, nested objects stay shared; use `structuredClone(o)`"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Interview: why is `[1]===[1]` false?** Two separate objects; `===` compares identity.",
                "**Does `const` make an object immutable?** No, only the binding.",
                "**Shallow vs deep copy?** Spread copies one level; `structuredClone` copies nested too."
              ],
              "style": "star",
              "ink": "purple"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "typeof Quirks",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "typeof Quirks",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What typeof returns",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`typeof` always returns a ==string==, never a type object",
                "Primitives: `'string'` `'number'` `'bigint'` `'boolean'` `'undefined'` `'symbol'`",
                "The other two: `'object'` and `'function'`"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. The traps",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Value",
                "typeof",
                "Right test"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`null`",
                  "{red:'object'} (legacy bug)",
                  "`x === null`"
                ],
                [
                  "`[]`",
                  "{red:'object'}",
                  "`Array.isArray(x)`"
                ],
                [
                  "`new Date()`",
                  "{red:'object'}",
                  "`x instanceof Date`"
                ],
                [
                  "`function(){}`",
                  "'function'",
                  "still an object"
                ],
                [
                  "`class A{}`",
                  "'function'",
                  "a class is a function"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Undeclared vs TDZ",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Undeclared name: `typeof` gives ==`'undefined'`==, **no error**",
                "`let`/`const` in its ==temporal dead zone==: throws `ReferenceError`"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "typeof nope;            // 'undefined'",
                "{ typeof x; let x = 1 } // ReferenceError"
              ],
              "note": "typeof is only safe for names never declared"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "`typeof` cannot tell {red:null}, arrays or dates from plain objects. Use `=== null` and `Array.isArray`."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "== vs ===",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "== vs ===",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Strict vs Loose",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`===` compares ==type and value==, no conversion",
                "`==` converts operands first (loose equality)",
                "{green:Default to `===`}",
                "`null == undefined` is true; nothing else equals them",
                "So `x == null` tests both in one go"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Loose Rules and Surprises",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "String vs number",
                    "sub": "string → number: '5'==5",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Boolean",
                    "sub": "→ number first: true==1",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Object vs primitive",
                    "sub": "ToPrimitive: [1]==1",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Expression",
                "Result",
                "Why"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`'' == 0`",
                  "true",
                  "'' → 0"
                ],
                [
                  "`'0' == false`",
                  "true",
                  "both → 0"
                ],
                [
                  "`'' == '0'`",
                  "false",
                  "two strings"
                ],
                [
                  "`[] == false`",
                  "true",
                  "'' → 0"
                ],
                [
                  "`[] == ![]`",
                  "true",
                  "both → 0"
                ],
                [
                  "`null == 0`",
                  "false",
                  "only undefined"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Object.is",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Pair",
                "===",
                "Object.is"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`NaN, NaN`",
                  "false",
                  "{green:true}"
                ],
                [
                  "`0, -0`",
                  "true",
                  "{red:false}"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Not transitive",
              "text": "`'' == 0` and `0 == '0'` are true, yet `'' == '0'` is ==false==."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Truthy, Falsy and Coercion Rules",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Truthy, Falsy and Coercion Rules",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Truthy and Falsy",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Exactly ==8 falsy==: `false` `0` `-0` `0n` `''` `null` `undefined` `NaN`",
                "Everything else is ==truthy==",
                "Surprise truthy: `'0'` `'false'` `[]` `{}` `function(){}` `new Boolean(false)` `-1` `Infinity`"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Coercion",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Value",
                "Number()",
                "Value",
                "Number()"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`''`",
                  "0",
                  "`null`",
                  "0"
                ],
                [
                  "`' 12 '`",
                  "12",
                  "`undefined`",
                  "NaN"
                ],
                [
                  "`'abc'`",
                  "NaN",
                  "`true`",
                  "1"
                ],
                [
                  "`[]`",
                  "0",
                  "`[5]`",
                  "5"
                ],
                [
                  "`{}`",
                  "NaN",
                  "",
                  ""
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`+` with any string ==concatenates==: `1+'2'` is `'12'`, `[1]+[2]` is `'12'`",
                "`- * / %` always ==convert to number==: `'6'-'2'` is 4, `'3'*'4'` is 12"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. || && ??",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`||` returns the first ==truthy== operand",
                "`&&` returns the first ==falsy== operand",
                "`??` skips only `null` and `undefined`"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "0 || 5   // 5",
                "0 ?? 5   // 0"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Defaults",
              "text": "Use ==??== when `0` or `''` are valid values."
            },
            {
              "type": "sidebox",
              "title": "Interview Point",
              "items": [
                "**Falsy count?** Eight; `[]` and `{}` are truthy",
                "**`Number(null)` vs `Number(undefined)`?** 0 vs NaN",
                "**`0 || 5` vs `0 ?? 5`?** 5 vs 0"
              ],
              "ink": "orange"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "null, undefined and NaN",
